## 1. Safe, Repeatable Test Data (`Q6`)

| Data Category | Authoritative Seed / Fixture Source | Isolation & Cleanup Strategy |
|---|---|---|
| **Roles & Tenants (`Role × Scope`)** | `{{auth_seed_source}}` | Created per test run / reset via `{{reset_cmd}}` |
| **Domain Records & State Preconditions** | `{{domain_seed_source}}` | Per-case transaction rollback or deterministic fixture cleanup |
| **Boundary & Malformed Payloads** | `{{boundary_fixture_source}}` | Read-only static fixtures |

### Non-Negotiable Data Rules
- **Zero production data**: Never copy production PII, live credentials, or customer snapshots into test fixtures.
- **Zero fabricated fallback data**: If a required seed source or dependency is unavailable, mark the affected test cases **`BLOCKED`** (`shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md`) — never hardcode fake "successful" fallback records.
- **Deterministic repeatability**: Every test case must be re-runnable back-to-back without manual database edits.

