## 2. Named Environments & External Provider Stubs (`Q7`)

| Case Group | Target Environment | External Provider Policy (`{{external_providers}}`) | Result Labelling |
|---|---|---|---|
| **API / Service Acceptance** | `{{api_env}}` | Real local/staging storage; external providers use sandbox or network-edge stub | `live` or `stubbed:<provider>` |
| **UI / Client End-to-End** | `{{ui_env}}` | Connected to `{{api_env}}` (or explicit contract-verified edge stub) | `live` or `stubbed:<provider>` |
| **Visual Fidelity** | `{{visual_env}}` | Deterministic fixture state for all 4 UI states | `baseline-compared` |

**Stub Rule (`Q7`)**: Stub external third-party providers only where authorized in the table above, always at the network/adapter boundary, and explicitly label every stubbed execution in the test report (`PASS (stubbed: <provider>)` never claims live third-party verification).

