## 4. Plan Review Rubric (`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`) & CLI Gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`)

Grade test plan review findings strictly with **`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`** and automated checks strictly with **`PASS` / `FAIL`** (`shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md`):

- **`BLOCKER`**: Any untestable AC left unescalated (`Q2`), any `{{ac_id_format}}` without a test case (`Q3`), missing `Role × Environment × Action × Object` permission or `SR14` hand-off coverage (`Q4`), expectations derived from implementation code (`Q14`), vague expected results (`Q11`), or production/fabricated fallback data (`Q6`).
- **`MAJOR`**: Missing validation, UI state, boundary, out-of-scope guard (`Q9`), or regression (`Q10`) coverage; UI End-to-End level chosen where API Acceptance suffices (`Q5`); unlabelled external stubs (`Q7`).
- **`MINOR`**: Case ordering, table formatting, or wording clarity that does not affect verification coverage.

Cross-check the deterministic CLI gates in `SKILL.md` (**G1–G3**) — all gates must report **`PASS`** and zero `BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` findings may remain open before handing the plan to `quality-acceptance`.

